 What is the most popular dish in Italy?

51
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:51,760
 And then maybe the playground is going to respond pizza and pasta.

52
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:55,520
 On top of it, this is just for the basic interactions,

53
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:58,720
 but we can have also knowledge bases or rag.

54
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,200
 And we'll have a full lecture dedicated to this.

55
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:03,440
 So don't worry if you don't understand it right now.

56
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:07,200
 But the idea is that we're going to be able to provide more relevant

57
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:11,920
 and more accurate responses by fetching data from external data sources

58
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:14,080
 that may have the answer for us.

59
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:18,160
 Don't worry, we'll have a deep dive into knowledge bases as well.

60
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,640
 We can fine tune our foundation model.

61
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:23,040
 That means that we're going to bring our own data

62
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:26,560
 and we're going to update the foundation model in our account again

63
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:31,920
 with our data to make sure that it's more adapted to our use case

64
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,440
 and our data.

65
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:38,240
 And finally, to access all of these things is going to be a unified API.

66
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,680
 So it's going to be the same for all models.

67
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,680
 That means that all your applications

68
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:44,160
 just took in one way to Amazon bedrock

69
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:47,200
 and then Amazon bedrock will do the magic for us.

